Description: Interactive and modular shiny app for single-cell and
    spatial transcriptomic data exploration and management. Visualize cell
    clusters or groups using interactive cell embeddings, e.g. UMAP or t-SNE,
    or spatial views. Explore cell composition and quality control metrics
    using the metadata viewer module. Investigate the effect of clustering
    resolutions or compare annotation sources using cluster tree. Visualize
    gene expression using cell embeddings or in spatial context with feature
    plots and coexpression plots or in cell clusters using dotplots, violin
    plots. Manage marker tables from single-cell or pseudo-bulk analyses and
    track genes of interest using the gene scratchpad. Choose interesting cells
    with lasso selection directly from interactive plots and export for
    downstream analysis. Slice and dice datasets with custom filters based on
    cell metadata, gene expression or lasso selections. Efficiently handle
    large datasets using custom downsampling controls. CascadeR has
    cross-ecosystem compatibility with support for Seurat, SingleCellExperiment
    and AnnData objects. In addition, the app includes an integrated platform
    to manage multiple projects and user access that can be run on a central
    server to share with collaborators.
